<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Puerto Rican Nationalist Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1922">1922</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Puerto Rican Nationalist Party was founded in 1922 to seek independence from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-albizu-campos">Pedro Albizu Campos</a> from 1930, turned to militant action. Police killed its marchers in the Ponce massacre of 1937, and its members led the uprisings of 1950 and the shooting in the US House of Representatives in 1954. Repression reduced it to a small movement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/puerto-rican-nationalist-party.jpg" alt="Puerto Rican Nationalist Party" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dariusofthedark · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Puerto_Rican_Nationalist_Party.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
